# Extraction artifacts — regenerated via `make l10n`.
# The per-locale runtime dictionaries under public/translations/ are
# committed so the app ships with translations; the intermediate
# per-file .kbf.json extract output is ephemeral and gitignored.
apps/kapi-desktop/frontend/i18n/
apps/kapi-desktop/frontend/i18n-qps/
apps/kapi-desktop/frontend/i18n-nb/

# Same policy for the bowrain UI surfaces (make bowrain-{app,ctrl,pulse}-translations):
# compiled public/translations/ dictionaries are committed, .kbf.json intermediates are not.
bowrain/packages/app/i18n/
bowrain/packages/app/i18n-qps/
bowrain/packages/app/i18n-nb/
bowrain/apps/ctrl/i18n/
bowrain/apps/ctrl/i18n-qps/
bowrain/apps/ctrl/i18n-nb/
bowrain/apps/pulse/i18n/
bowrain/apps/pulse/i18n-qps/
bowrain/apps/pulse/i18n-nb/

# Same policy for the transactional emails (make l10n): the committed
# artifacts are the rendered per-locale templates under
# bowrain/mailer/templates/ and subject catalogs under bowrain/mailer/subjects/;
# the KBF extraction, per-locale intermediates, compiled catalogs, and the
# per-locale esbuild render bundles are ephemeral.
bowrain/emails/i18n/
bowrain/emails/i18n-qps/
bowrain/emails/i18n-nb/
bowrain/emails/translations/
bowrain/emails/.render/

# Landing page (make l10n): the compiled runtime catalogs under
# bowrain/web/landing/translations/ are committed (web-landing.yml builds the
# nb variant from them); the KBF extraction intermediates are ephemeral.
bowrain/web/landing/i18n/
bowrain/web/landing/i18n-qps/
bowrain/web/landing/i18n-nb/

# Docusaurus target-locale docs are GENERATED by the root kapi.yaml dogfood
# recipe (web/docs/** -> web/i18n/<locale>/), so they're build artefacts, not
# source. Committing them made every source-doc edit go stale and hard-fail the
# nb build — see CLAUDE.md "Target-language drift must never block the build".
# Regenerate with kapi; the nb locale falls back to English until then.
web/i18n/nb/
# The qps pseudo-locale for both Docusaurus sites. Generated by
# scripts/pseudo-docs-i18n.sh immediately before each site build (see
# .github/actions/pseudo-locale) and never committed: it is a pure function of
# the docs, changes with every docs edit, and runs to ~450 files. Committing it
# means a large diff on every docs PR, or a probe that goes stale — and a stale
# probe LIES, because a page added since the last run falls back to English and
# reads as "not translatable" when it means "not regenerated".
web/i18n/qps/
bowrain/web/docs/i18n/qps/
# The React tier of the same generation: extracted blocks and the compiled
# dictionary the build-time transform reads. Same reasoning as the qps trees
# above — a pure function of the source, regenerated per build.
web/i18n-kbf/
web/i18n-runtime/
# Same policy for the bowrain docs site: the bowrain-docs surface of the root
# recipe generates bowrain/web/docs/i18n/<locale>/ from bowrain/web/docs/docs/**
# (make l10n). Build artefact, never committed; the nb locale
# falls back to English until regenerated.
bowrain/web/docs/i18n/nb/

# The Go surfaces keep gettext MO as the runtime format, but a compiled catalog
# is build output: `go run ./core/i18n/gen/catalogs` produces each <locale>.mo
# from the committed <locale>.json beside it, ahead of anything that compiles
# core/i18n or host/i18n. Version control carries the reviewable JSON; a binary
# nobody can read in a diff is how corrupt bytes got committed unnoticed.
core/i18n/catalogs/*.mo
host/i18n/catalogs/*.mo

# Dogfood project state for the root kapi.yaml recipe.
#
# `.kapi/` is committed, so only the two things that are not get named here, and
# they are the same two `kapi init` writes into `.kapi/.gitignore` (see
# core/project.StateGitignore). Everything else in there is authored: the
# manifest, the flows, and the context sources — the terms bundle, the memory
# seeds, the brand voice, and the decision record, which belongs in the change
# that caused the drift and must reconcile on a fresh clone with no server.
#
# Two plain paths, no `/.kapi/*` star and no negation clawing anything back:
# git does not descend into an ignored directory, so a negation inside one
# never matches.
/.kapi/work/
/.kapi/filters.local.json
# A `kapi memory`/`kapi terms` run with no --file/--name defaults to --local,
# which writes these into the working directory. They are rebuildable state, not
# source (AD-009/AD-010), so they must never be committed. The names track
# core/project.MemoryFileName and TermsFileName; the pre-#1504/#1522 spellings
# (tm.db, termbase.db) matched nothing here any more.
/memory.db
/terms.db
# Disposable TMX/CSV review views of the native l10n seeds (l10n-review-export).
/l10n/review/

# Strategy and audit notes live in the private strategy repo under
# $NEOKAPI_WORKSPACE_DIR, never here: this repo is public, and a security audit
# carries reproductions for vulnerabilities that may still be unfixed. One was
# swept in at the repo root once (#1520); anchored so a working copy at the root
# cannot be staged again.
/kimi-evaluation.md

